Subject: [PATCH 13/24] Test the WAL limit across a transaction, a reopen and a
 shared connection

Implementation note 8: the limit is checked when a write starts, so an
explicit transaction whose writes started below it commits past it; past
it, a transaction still starts and reads, its write throws and it rolls
back. Engines that know nothing of earlier refusals (a reopen, a shared
connection) refuse writes the same way, with neither file changed, until a
data sync succeeds; then a write is accepted, a checkpoint drains the WAL,
and a power loss keeps every row.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
